use std
into strand_test.amni

Imports: os, binary, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion and gfx.scene3d.

Struct `HairU` holds view_proj, view and proj (each `gfx::mat4`), then size, cam, to_sun, sun_rgb, hair, sky, params and look (each `float4`), then light_vp (`gfx::mat4`), light (`float4`) and shadow_vp (`gfx::mat4`), in that order, matching the GLSL uniform block `Hair` in shaders/strand_common.glsl.

`real_arg(s const byte[:]) f32` parses one argument string as a real and returns it `as f32`; callers pass `a[i]`.

`main()` renders a character without its hair cards through `s3d` and then draws strand hair over it with compute shaders. With `a = args()`: `a[1]` the .glb path, `a[2]` the guides file path, `a[3]` the output .png path, `a[4]`..`a[6]` eye x y z and `a[7]`..`a[9]` target x y z (each read as `real_arg(a[i])`), `a[10]` strands per card as an int. Size 768 by 1024. Open headless with `gfx::open_headless(768, 1024)` (on failure print "gpu: skipped (no device: " plus `gfx::error()` plus ")" and return). Load the glb with `gltf::load` (negative: print "load failed: " plus `gltf::error()` and return), add it with `s3d::add` and place the returned item at the origin with `s3d::place(item, gfx::translate(float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }))`. Set `s3d::view` to an `s3d::Camera` from eye to target, up (0, 1, 0), fov_y 0.5, near 0.02, far 60; set `s3d::sun.shadows = true`; `s3d::init(768, 1024)`; make `scene = gfx::render_target(768, 1024, gfx::RGBA8)` and call `s3d::render(scene)` three times.
Read the guides file with the unqualified `read_file(path, data)` (from os, no namespace prefix) into a `byte[>..]` list (on failure print "guides failed" and return). Its layout: 4 magic bytes "HMG2", then three little-endian i32 (guides, points, segments) at bytes 4, 8 and 12, then points × 48 bytes of point data, then segments × 16 bytes of segment data. Make `pts = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 48, <the point bytes slice>)` and `segs = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, segments * 16, <the segment bytes slice>)`, a `zeros byte[>..]` of 768*1024*64 zero bytes (resize it), then `front = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, 768*1024*4, zeros[..768*1024*4])` and `acc = gfx::buffer(<same usage>, 768*1024*64, zeros[..])` (gfx::buffer always takes three arguments). Make light buffers the same way at 512 by 512: `lfront` of 512*512*4 bytes and `lacc` of 512*512*64 bytes (slices of `zeros`). Make `outt = gfx::texture(gfx::TextureDesc { format: gfx::RGBA8, usage: gfx::SAMPLED | gfx::COMPUTE_WRITE, width: 768, height: 1024 })` and `smp = gfx::sampler(gfx::NEAREST, gfx::CLAMP)`. Build three compute pipelines with `gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_clear.comp"))`, `"shaders/strand_raster.comp"` and `"shaders/strand_resolve.comp"`.
Fill a `HairU` u: view_proj `s3d::view_proj_nj`, view `s3d::view_mat`, proj `s3d::proj_mat`; size (768, 1024, strands per card `as f32`, segments `as f32`); cam (eye xyz, 0.7); to_sun the normalized `s3d::sun.to_sun` with w 0; sun_rgb `s3d::sun.rgb` with w 0; hair (0.58, 0.38, 0.14, 0.42); sky (0.12, 0.13, 0.15, 40.0); params (0.004, 1.7, 0.004, 0.00007); look (1.0, 6.0, 0.0, 0.7). For the light: `center` is the mean of the first three f32 of every point (decode each little-endian f32 from the point bytes, point k at byte 16 + k*48, with `binary::f32_from_bits(<u32 little-endian> as u32)`, importing `binary`); `ld` is the normalized `s3d::sun.to_sun`; `leye = center + ld * 3.0`; light_vp is `gfx::mul(gfx::perspective(0.24, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0), gfx::look_at(leye, center, float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }))`; light is (512, 512, 0.35, 256 / tan(0.12)) all `as f32`; shadow_vp is `s3d::cascade_vp[0]`.
Each compute pass is opened with `gfx::begin_compute` and closed with `gfx::end_compute()`; bind the pipeline with `gfx::bind`, then set `u.look.z` to the pass mode and call `gfx::uniforms(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, u)`. A helper `raster(rw0, rw1, ro0, ro1, mode)` (a nested fn or a local block you repeat) runs one raster pass: read-write buffers [rw0, rw1], raster pipeline, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, s3d::nd_target(), smp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 1, s3d::shadow_map, smp)`, `gfx::bind_storage_buffer(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, pts)`, `(gfx::COMPUTE, 1, segs)`, `(gfx::COMPUTE, 2, ro0)`, `(gfx::COMPUTE, 3, ro1)`, mode, dispatch ((segments + 63) / 64, strands per card, 1). Passes in order: clear with read-write [front, acc] mode 0 dispatching ((768*1024 + 63) / 64, 1, 1); clear with [lfront, lacc] mode 2 dispatching ((512*512 + 63) / 64, 1, 1); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 2); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 3); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 0); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 1); then the resolve: read-write buffers none and read-write textures [outt] (the two-list `gfx::begin_compute`), resolve pipeline, mode 1, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, scene, smp)`, `gfx::bind_storage_buffer(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, acc)`, dispatch ((768 + 7) / 8, (1024 + 7) / 8, 1). Then `gfx::save_png(outt, path)` and print "saved " plus the path, or print "error: " plus `gfx::error()` when it fails.
